From: Sonata AGENTS <sonata@pypto-sonata>
Date: 2026-06-27
Subject: [PATCH] aicpu_executor: add Sonata schedule branch at orchestrator call

Adds a conditional branch at the orchestrator thread's ``(*p_func)(orch_args)``
call site.  When ``Runtime::sonata_sched_addr_`` is non-zero, a precomputed
FlatSchedule binary is available and the orchestrator delegates to
``sonata_orchestrate_with_schedule()`` instead of invoking the standard
orchestration SO.

Also exports the orch function pointer + args globally so the sonata path
can delegate to TMARB after entering the sonata code path (C2 PROOF).

Zero default (``sonata_sched_addr_ == 0``) -> TMARB behaviour unchanged.
Part of Sonata NPU dual-path integration (ADR-002).


diff --git a/src/a2a3/runtime/tensormap_and_ringbuffer/aicpu/aicpu_executor.cpp b/src/a2a3/runtime/tensormap_and_ringbuffer/aicpu/aicpu_executor.cpp
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/a2a3/runtime/tensormap_and_ringbuffer/aicpu/aicpu_executor.cpp
+++ b/src/a2a3/runtime/tensormap_and_ringbuffer/aicpu/aicpu_executor.cpp
@@ -564,7 +564,25 @@
             framework_bind_runtime(rt);
             if (*p_bind != nullptr) {
                 (*p_bind)(rt);
             }
+
+            // Export orch function + args so sonata_orchestrate can
+            // delegate to TMARB after entering the sonata code path.
+            extern void sonata_set_orch_fn(void *fn, void *args);
+            sonata_set_orch_fn(reinterpret_cast<void *>(*p_func),
+                               reinterpret_cast<void *>(&orch_args_cached_));
+
             rt_scope_begin(rt);
-            (*p_func)(*orch_args_cached_);
+            // Sonata schedule branch (ADR-002): try interpreter first.
+            // Returns true if a schedule was found and executed; false means
+            // fall back to the standard TMARB orchestrator path.
+            extern "C" bool sonata_orchestrate_with_schedule(
+                PTO2Runtime* rt, Runtime* runtime
+            );
+            if (!sonata_orchestrate_with_schedule(rt, runtime)) {
+                (*p_func)(*orch_args_cached_);
+            }
             rt_scope_end(rt);
